{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>The hand of a ger and toshav.</b> A ger who is a toshav — as the Targum renders: עָרֵל תּוֹתָב; and the end of the verse proves it — ״וְנִמְכַּר לְגֵר תּוֹשָׁב.״" "<b>And when the hand of a ger and toshav with you attains.</b> What caused him to become rich? His attachment with you." "<b>And your brother is impoverished with him.</b> What caused him to become impoverished? His attachment with him — because he learned from his deeds." "<b>The family of a ger.</b> This is the nation — when it says לְעֵקֶר, this means sold to it itself, to be its servant, and not for divinity but to chop wood and draw water (Sifra; Bava Kamma 113)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {3 "לְעֵקֶר ('for the root/itself') appears to be a technical midrashic term; translated hyper-literally. The intent: the ger is sold to the nation as a body, for menial service, not as idolatrous consecration."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:34.187395224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}